MDT until November 4 at 5:00AM MST by NWS Pueblo CO","description":"* WHAT...Flooding caused by excessive rainfall will be possible,\nespecially over the western half of San Luis Valley.\n\n* WHERE...The western half of the San Luis Valley, including Del\nNorte, Antonito and Mogote.\n\n* WHEN...From Sunday afternoon through late Tuesday night.\n\n* IMPACTS...Excessive runoff may result in flooding of rivers,\ncreeks, streams, and other low-lying and flood-prone location.\n\n* ADDITIONAL DETAILS...\n- Runoff from heavy rain and melting snow over the San Juan\nMountains may cause flooding in the San Luis Valley, especially\nMonday and Tuesday as high flows move out of the mountains and\nthrough the Rio Grande and Conejos River.\n- The greatest risk of flooding will be along the Conejos River and\nthe Rio Grande, including Del Norte and Mogote.\n- http://www.weather.gov/safety/flood","ends":"2026-11-04T06:00:00-06:00","severity":"Severe","areaDesc":"Del Norte Vicinity/Northern San Luis Valley Below 8500 Ft; Alamosa  Vicinity/Central San Luis Valley Below 8500 Ft; Southern San Luis Valley","id":"urn:oid:2.49.0.1.840.0.6c702f44556c2240320a73dcc302b9a6b4962366.001.1","url":"https://api.weather.gov/alerts/urn:oid:2.49.0.1.840.0.6c702f44556c2240320a73dcc302b9a6b4962366.001.1"},{"event":"Winter Storm Watch","headline":"Winter Storm Watch issued October 30 at 11:17AM MDT until November 2 at 11:00AM MST by NWS Pueblo CO","description":"* WHAT...Heavy snow possible. Total snow accumulations between 8 and\n14 inches possible. Winds could gust as high as 55 mph.\n\n* WHERE...Eastern San Juan Mountains Above 10000 Feet County.\n\n* WHEN...From Sunday afternoon through Monday morning.\n\n* IMPACTS...Travel could be very difficult, especially Sunday night\nand Monday morning. Strong winds could produce areas of blowing and\ndrifting snow.","ends":"2026-11-02T12:00:00-06:00","severity":"Severe","areaDesc":"Eastern San Juan Mountains Above 10000 Ft","id":"urn:oid:2.49.0.1.840.0.bc72b7